  "final_answer": "I have gathered enough information now to provide a comprehensive answer.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Parking Lot Found: LAZ Parking - The 1 Hotel Brooklyn Bridge Garage**\n- **Address:** 60 Furman St, Brooklyn, NY 11201\n- **Hours:** Open 24 hours ✓\n- **Phone:** +1 347-599-2922\n- **Website:** lazparking.com\n\n### Rating Overview\n- **Overall Rating:** 3.1 stars (out of 61 reviews)\n- Rating distribution is highly polarized:\n  - ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (5 stars): 27 reviews\n  - ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4 stars): 6 reviews\n  - ⭐⭐⭐ (3 stars): 2 reviews\n  - ⭐⭐ (2 stars): 0 reviews\n  - ⭐ (1 star): 26 reviews\n\n### Common Review Themes (filters on the page)\n- **价格 (Price):** 9 reviews\n- **付款 (Payment):** 3 reviews\n- **人民 (People):** 2 reviews\n- **骗子 (Scam):** 2 reviews\n- **30分钟 (30 minutes):** 2 reviews\n\n### Notable User Comments\n\n| Reviewer | Rating | Time | Summary |\n|----------|--------|------|---------|\n| **I D** (3 photos) | 1★ | 1 month ago | Negative review; owner replied |\n| **Ezmar Rivera** (Local Guide) | 1★ | 3 months ago | \"I don't recommend this place. We were told to wait, then the owner came, made us move, and treated us like trash. He yelled at us, was rude to my daughter, and threatened to hit me.\" (Owner replied) |\n| **Grégoire Leleu** | 1★ | 5 months ago | \"I'm also one of the victims of this place. We returned on time, but the guy kept us waiting and charged us double.\" (Owner replied) |\n| **Prophetgu3** (Local Guide, 309 reviews) | 3★ | 1 year ago | \"Last Friday night I went to pick up the car, waited 30 minutes. The employee saw me waiting with my ticket and brazenly took keys from other customers in front of me.\" (Owner replied) |\n| **Paola Garay** | 1★ | 10 months ago | \"They are scammers. They lie to get you to park, quote one price and change it when you pay. The worst part is they change their story when confronted.\" |\n| **Frank III** | 1★ | 1 year ago | Complaints about overcharging for extra half-hour; lost as a customer (Owner replied) |\n| **William Gentile** | 1★ | 1 year ago | \"Can I give zero stars? Price is outrageous, they misled me. They charged me $90 for 8 hours! Do NOT go!\" |\n| **Alex** (Local Guide, photos) | 1★ | 2 years ago | \"Waited 30 minutes to pick up the car, and the valet wouldn't give me the keys unless I tipped.\" |\n| **Denni Wibowo** (Local Guide, 664 reviews) | 1★ | 8 months ago | \"Watch the price. Actual price differs from listed. The attendant said minimum charge is $62.50 for 3 hours (different from Spot Hero listing).\" |\n| **GURASEES Singh** | 1★ | 2 years ago | Poor communication at the counter regarding oversized vehicle charges (Owner replied) |\n\n### Key Takeaways from Reviews\nThe reviews are predominantly **negative** with consistent complaints about:\n- 💰 **Excessive pricing & overcharging** (most common complaint)\n- ⏱️ **Long 30-minute waits** for vehicle pickup\n- 🎯 **Price discrepancies** between quoted, listed, and final amounts\n- 🅿️ **Unprofessional staff** — accusations of intimidation, threats, and aggressive demands for tips before keys would be returned\n- 🚨 **Accusations of scamming**\n\nThe owner has responded to most negative reviews, but the polar distribution (27 five-star vs. 26 one-star reviews) suggests customer experiences vary wildly.",
